From a0fe7e285a63b6ca1ef53f27bb8220bd5b2b8480 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): preserve waits before rehomed history arrives
 [daveey]

Task rows become visible before history pages during owner rehome. Recovery relied exclusively on blocked events, so an unanswered human_request could promote; first-park absence also looked like a legacy missing wake. Read stored asks as sticky, and anchor missing-first-park grace on the existing local restore receipt rather than old imported event clocks. Existing explicit unblock clears the ask; imported park deadlines and bounded missing-park recovery remain intact.

Proof: actual remote apply between task/history pages reproduces 2 human promotion failures and 2 scheduled-state failures before fixes. New tests plus remote-repark controls pass; scripts/check --base origin/main passes. Full Kanban regression and independent canonical review/CI required before landing. Live containment remains separate; no human answers or acceptance waivers inferred.
